# Language conventions (Cosmo Pug)

## Chat with the user

- Write **all assistant replies in Ukrainian** ( explanations, summaries, questions, status updates).

## Everything in the repository

Use **English** unless the user explicitly asks for another language in a specific file:

- Source code, identifiers, and comments
- README and other docs
- In-game UI strings (HUD, menus, game over, tutorials)
- Commit messages and PR text (when the user asks you to write them)
- Xcode project display names and `Info.plist` user-facing strings

## Examples

```swift
// ✅ GOOD — UI copy in English
scoreLabel.text = "Score: \(score)"

// ❌ BAD — Ukrainian in the game UI
scoreLabel.text = "Очки: \(score)"
```

When adding localized strings later, default to English as the base (`en`) and add `uk` (or others) via `Localizable.strings` only if requested.
